    "https://www.caldwell.edu/hr/employment-opportunities/faculty-adjunct/": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Computer Science (Req. #2428)",
      "description": "Faculty Positions – Adjunct – Caldwell University Faculty Positions – Adjunct – Caldwell University Caldwell University Caldwell University is a private, accredited Catholic university in Caldwell, NJ offering bachelor's, master's and doctoral degrees and a vibrant campus life complete with rewarding activities, clubs, and service opportunities. Skip to content Information For Alumni Current Students Faculty and Staff Parents High School Counselors Academics Mega Menu Column Left Column Academics Overview Academic Services Degrees & Programs Schools Cougar One Stop Centers & Institutes Library Research & Special Programs Caldwell is consistently ranked as a \"Best College\" by the U.S. News & World Report. Explore Degrees Admissions Mega Menu Column Left Column Admissions Overview Graduate Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Apply Now Transfer Students Visit Us International Admissions Accepted Students 95% of grads are employed, in grad school, or committed to service within 6 months of graduation Apply Today! Cost & Aid Mega Menu Column Left Column Cost & Aid Overview Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Scholarships & Grants Net Price Calculator Cougar One Stop The “Caldwell Commitment” program provides aid to students entering Caldwell University based on academic merit and financial needs. Learn more Campus Life Mega Menu Column Left Column Campus Life Overview Housing & Dining Clubs & Organizations Campus Safety Campus Ministry Athletics Recreational Sports Fitness Center Health & Wellness Cougar Express 14 NCAA Division II Athletics Programs View Athletics Who We Are Mega Menu Column Left Column Who We Are President Core Values & History Board of Trustees Strategic Plan Consumer Information News & Events Getting Here Faculty & Staff Directory Alumni Information Located just 22 miles from NYC and one hour from the Jersey Shore, Caldwell was rated as the \"Best College Town in NJ.\" Discover Caldwell Athletics Apply Visit Give Search Box Close Popular Searches admissions degree visit-us [elyee子] [44p - 141mb] 东方project 十六夜咲夜 Popular Searches Degree Admissions Apply Now Visit Us Explore Caldwell Admissions Degree Programs Financial Aid Visit Campus Current Students My Caldwell Bookstore Library Cougar Apps & Email Prospective Students Admissions Degree Programs Financial Aid Admissions Counselors Apply Visit Close Search Faculty Positions – Adjunct Human Resources Employment Opportunities Faculty Positions – Adjunct In this section Employment Opportunities Administration – Executive Administration – Full-Time Office Support Staff Positions Administration – Part-Time Athletics Positions – Full-Time Athletics Positions – Part-Time Faculty Positions – Full-Time Faculty Positions – Adjunct Faculty Positions – Part-Time Equal Employment Opportunities Caldwell University is committed to recruiting and retaining faculty, staff, and students who will further the traditions, goals, and core values of the University in support of our Catholic Dominican mission, vision, and strategic plan. Caldwell seeks employees who are committed to contributing to an energetic, welcoming atmosphere. Caldwell University is a private, Catholic coed four-year university with a strong liberal arts core curriculum that enhances critical thinking and analytical reasoning. Caldwell offers 36 undergraduate and 31 graduate programs, including doctoral, master’s, certificate, and certification programs, as well as online and distance learning options that prepare students for today’s global marketplace. The university has 15 NCAA Division II athletic teams and numerous clubs, fraternities, sororities, and activities on a beautiful 70-acre campus located in the suburbs of Caldwell, New Jersey. Caldwell was founded by the Sisters of Saint Dominic of Caldwell. Its core values of respect, integrity, community, and excellence influence academic and campus life. For more information about Caldwell University, visit caldwell.edu . Caldwell University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Caldwell University offers the following benefits to part-time adjuncts that include: Paid sick leave Retirement Savings: 403(b) supplemental retirement annuity plan Adjunct Instructor, Computer Science (Req. #2428) Salary: $2,600.00 Annually The School of Business and Computer Science at Caldwell University invites applications for its Computer Science and Information Systems Adjunct Faculty Pool. The purpose of the pool is to identify qualified instructors whom the School can contact as teaching needs arise for on-campus undergraduate courses at Caldwell University in Caldwell, New Jersey. We are seeking qualified, motivated educators with academic and/or professional expertise in areas including: Computer Programming Programming Language Paradigms Data Structures, Algorithms Front-end Web Development, Full-stack Web Development Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, LLM integration in software (AI Engineering) Cybersecurity, Networking, Data Security Database Management Data Science Management Information Systems Linux/OS/Cloud Management, Computer Architecture Software Engineering, System Analysis and Design, AI-assisted development Data and Computational Applications We are particularly interested in faculty who bring relevant professional and technical experience into the classroom and are committed to student success and excellence in teaching. Applicants should review the Caldwell University undergraduate catalog and identify the specific Computer Science and Information Systems courses they are qualified and interested in teaching . Applicants should also indicate whether they are available to teach during the day, in the evening, or both . Qualifications Master’s degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, Information Technology, Cybersecurity, Data Science, or a closely related field required; doctorate preferred Relevant professional and technical experience strongly valued Prior college-level teaching experience strongly valued Strong communication and organizational skills Responsibilities Adjunct faculty selected for teaching assignments will be expected to: Teach assigned courses in accordance with School and University guidelines Prepare and deliver engaging instruction, assignments, and assessments Provide students with timely feedback and appropriate availability outside of class Assess student learning and submit grades and required documentation in a timely manner Support the mission and academic standards of Caldwell University Application Process Applicants should submit: Curriculum vitae or resume Cover letter identifying: The specific Caldwell University Computer Science and Information Systems courses they are qualified and interested in teaching Relevant academic and professional expertise Availability to teach during the day, in the evening, or both Unofficial transcripts Contact information for professional references Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis. Qualified applicants will be added to the Computer Science and Information Systems Adjunct Faculty Pool and may be contacted when teaching opportunities matching their qualifications and availability arise. Placement in the adjunct pool does not guarantee a teaching assignment. Apply Now Adjunct Instructor, Business Adjuncts (Req. #2427) Salary: $2,600.00 Annually The School of Business and Computer Science at Caldwell University invites applications for its Business Adjunct Faculty Pool. The purpose of the pool is to identify qualified instructors whom the School can contact as teaching needs arise for on-campus undergraduate business courses at Caldwell University in Caldwell, New Jersey. We are seeking qualified, motivated educators with academic and/or professional expertise in areas including: Business Business Communications Artificial Intelligence in Business Sport Management Finance Accounting Healthcare Administration Human Resource Management International Business Leadership and Management Marketing and Digital Marketing Business Spreadsheets We are particularly interested in faculty who bring relevant professional experience into the classroom and are committed to student success and excellence in teaching. Applicants should review the Caldwell University undergraduate catalog and identify the specific business courses they are qualified and interested in teaching . Applicants should also indicate whether they are available to teach during the day, in the evening, or both . Qualifications Master’s degree in the relevant discipline required; doctorate preferred Relevant professional experience is strongly valued Prior college-level teaching experience is strongly valued Strong communication and organizational skills Responsibilities Adjunct faculty selected for teaching assignments will be expected to: Teach assigned courses in accordance with School and University guidelines Prepare and deliver engaging instruction, assignments, and assessments Provide students with timely feedback and appropriate availability outside of class Assess student learning and submit grades and required documentation in a timely manner Support the mission and academic standards of Caldwell University Application Process Applicants should submit: Curriculum vitae or resume Cover letter identifying: The specific Caldwell University business courses they are qualified and interested in teaching Relevant academic and professional expertise Availability to teach during the day, in the evening, or both Unofficial transcripts Contact information for professional references Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis. Qualified applicants will be added to the Business Adjunct Faculty Pool and may be contacted when teaching opportunities matching their qualifications and availability arise. Placement in the adjunct pool does not guarantee a teaching assignment. Apply Now In this section Employment Opportunities Administration – Executive Administration – Full-Time Office Support Staff Positions Administration – Part-Time Athletics Positions – Full-Time Athletics Positions – Part-Time Faculty Positions – Full-Time Faculty Positions – Adjunct Faculty Positions – Part-Time Equal Employment Opportunities Caldwell University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national and ethnic origin, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law in administration of its educational policies, admissions policies, scholarship and loan programs, and athletic and other school-administered programs. Academics Degrees & Programs Academic Calendar Summer Session Course Search Undergrad Catalog Graduate Catalog Registrar Community About Caldwell Campus Life Cougar Alumni Helpful Links Cougar One Stop Caldwell University Student Handbook Campus Store Corporate Partnerships Employment Give to Caldwell News Title IX and Anti-Harassment and Discrimination Policy Student Consumer Information Digital Millennium Copyright Act Privacy Policy 120 Bloomfield Avenue, Caldwell, NJ 07006 Map & Directions Contact Us Website Accessibility Request Info Schedule a Visit Caldwell University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national and ethnic origin, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law in administration of its educational policies, admissions policies, scholarship and loan programs, and athletic and other school-administered programs. ©2026        Caldwell University Privacy Policy Caldwell University is proudly powered by WordPress round-tick-outline round-tick-fill tick double-tick round-cross-outline round-cross-fill cross vertical-three-dots three-horizontal-dots three-horizontal-dots triangle-left triangle-up triangle-right triangle-down arrow-left arrow-up arrow-right arrow-down refresh mic round-minus-outline round-minus-fill minus round-plus-outline round-plus-fill plus chat-outline chat-fill message-outline message-fill bell-outline bell-fill bookmark-outline bookmark-fill folder-outline folder-fill f